doc:sch-1-sec-13a a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "13A After subsection 35(3)" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Insert:  (3A) Subsection (2) does not prevent an officer from divulging or communicating IPO information to an IGIS official if:  (a) the information is relevant to the functions or powers of the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security; and  (b) the Ombudsman is satisfied on reasonable grounds that the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security has satisfactory arrangements in place for protecting the information.  Schedule 1  Amendments" ;
    cof:pageNumber "15"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-13b a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "13B At the end of section 35"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-13b ;
    values:originalText "Add:  (9) In this section: Australian Designated Authority has the same meaning as in Schedule 1 to the Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979. Australian Designated Authority official means:  (a) the Australian Designated Authority; or  (b) a person who:  (i) is an APS employee in the Department administered by the Attorney-General; and  (ii) has duties relating to the functions or powers of the Australian Designated Authority under Schedule 1 to the Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979. IGIS official has the same meaning as in the Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979. IPO information means:  (a) protected information within the meaning of Schedule 1 to the Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979; or  (b) information relevant to the operation of that Schedule.  Amendments  Schedule 1 General amendments  Part 1  No. 78, 2021 Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production Orders) Act 2021  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979" ;
    skos:definition "Add:  (9) In this section: Australian Designated Authority has the same meaning as in Schedule 1 to the Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979. Australian Designated Authority official means:  (a) the Australian Designated Authority; or  (b) a person who:  (i) is an APS employee in the Department administered by the Attorney-General; and  (ii) has duties relating to the functions or powers of the Australian Designated Authority under Schedule 1 to the Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979. IGIS official has the same meaning as in the Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979. IPO information means:  (a) protected information within the meaning of Schedule 1 to the Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979; or  (b) information relevant to the operation of that Schedule.  Amendments  Schedule 1 General amendments  Part 1  No. 78, 2021 Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production Orders) Act 2021  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "8f3d2713595ab91dbe578dc1bf4a004a5b328a6ff7d31bdba8f9c14e82dbd33f" ;
    cof:pageNumber "16"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Definitions for Australian Designated Authority and IPO information" ;
