concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-4-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "4 Message application service"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-4-2 ;
    values:originalText "(1) For the purposes of this Schedule, message application service means a service that enables end-users to send or receive messages to or from other end-users using a transmission service.  (2) For the purposes of subclause (1), it is immaterial whether the service also enables end-users to send or receive messages to or from persons (other than end-users) using a transmission service. Example: A webmail service that enables end-users to send emails to, or receive emails from, any email address.  (3) For the purposes of this Schedule, a person does not provide a message application service merely because the person supplies a transmission service that enables messages to be sent or received.  Amendments  Schedule 1 General amendments  Part 1  No. 78, 2021 Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production Orders) Act 2021  (4) For the purposes of this Schedule, a person does not provide a message application service merely because the person provides a billing service, or a fee collection service, in relation to a message application service." ;
    skos:definition "(1) For the purposes of this Schedule, message application service means a service that enables end-users to send or receive messages to or from other end-users using a transmission service.  (2) For the purposes of subclause (1), it is immaterial whether the service also enables end-users to send or receive messages to or from persons (other than end-users) using a transmission service. Example: A webmail service that enables end-users to send emails to, or receive emails from, any email address.  (3) For the purposes of this Schedule, a person does not provide a message application service merely because the person supplies a transmission service that enables messages to be sent or received.  Amendments  Schedule 1 General amendments  Part 1  No. 78, 2021 Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production Orders) Act 2021  (4) For the purposes of this Schedule, a person does not provide a message application service merely because the person provides a billing service, or a fee collection service, in relation to a message application service."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "45f01ec88ac35096eb2572a0c251c241c44683848b35b5eb6e32cf80469f3968" ;
    cof:pageNumber "38"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-4-2-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-4-2-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-4-2-ss-3 ;
