    values:originalText "(1) For the purposes of this Schedule, eligible Judge means a Judge in relation to whom a consent under subclause (2) and a declaration under subclause (3) are in force.  (2) A Judge may, by writing, consent to be nominated by the Attorney-General under subclause (3).  (3) The Attorney-General may, by writing, declare Judges in relation to whom consents are in force under subclause (2) to be eligible Judges for the purposes of this Schedule.  (4) An eligible Judge has, in relation to the performance or exercise of a function or power conferred on an eligible Judge by this Schedule, the same protection and immunity as a Justice of the High Court has in relation to proceedings in the High Court." ;
