doc:sch-1-sec-22-2-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "22(3) Application for international production order—enforcement of" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) The application must be made on the interception agency’s behalf by:  (a) in the case of the Australian Federal Police—a member of the Australian Federal Police; or  (b) in the case of the Australian Commission for Law Enforcement Integrity:  (i) the Integrity Commissioner; or  (ii) an Assistant Integrity Commissioner; or  (iii) a staff member of the Australian Commission for Law Enforcement Integrity who is authorised in writing by the Integrity Commissioner for the purposes of this paragraph; or  (c) in the case of the ACC:  (i) the Chief Executive Officer of the ACC or an examiner; or  (ii) a member of a police force who is a member of the staff of the ACC; or  Schedule 1  Amendments" ;
    cof:pageNumber "49"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-23-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "23 Form of application"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-23-2 ;
    values:originalText "(1) Subject to subclause (2), an application under clause 22 for an international production order must be in writing.  (2) If the person making an application under clause 22 for an international production order on an interception agency’s behalf:  (a) is the chief officer of the agency or a person in relation to whom an authorisation by the chief officer is in force under subclause (3); and  Amendments  Schedule 1 General amendments  Part 1  No. 78, 2021 Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production Orders) Act 2021  (b) thinks it necessary, because of urgent circumstances, to make the application by telephone; the person may make the application by telephone. Note: See also clause 17A (urgent circumstances) and clause 172 (action required).  (3) The chief officer of an interception agency may authorise in writing, for the purposes of subclause (2), persons who, or classes of persons who, are entitled under clause 22 to make applications on the agency’s behalf." ;
    skos:definition "(1) Subject to subclause (2), an application under clause 22 for an international production order must be in writing.  (2) If the person making an application under clause 22 for an international production order on an interception agency’s behalf:  (a) is the chief officer of the agency or a person in relation to whom an authorisation by the chief officer is in force under subclause (3); and  Amendments  Schedule 1 General amendments  Part 1  No. 78, 2021 Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production Orders) Act 2021  (b) thinks it necessary, because of urgent circumstances, to make the application by telephone; the person may make the application by telephone. Note: See also clause 17A (urgent circumstances) and clause 172 (action required).  (3) The chief officer of an interception agency may authorise in writing, for the purposes of subclause (2), persons who, or classes of persons who, are entitled under clause 22 to make applications on the agency’s behalf."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "feb5495bb7b0861951fcda8fcd3bc64b5b7cbd69df94b98f50344e10dd2c09ed" ;
    cof:pageNumber "50"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-23-2-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-23-2-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-23-2-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
