concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-30-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "30 Issue of international production order—enforcement of the"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-30-2 ;
    values:originalText "criminal law Scope  (1) This clause applies if an interception agency applies, under clause 22, to an eligible Judge or nominated AAT member for an international production order that:  (a) is in respect of:  (i) one or more individual transmission services; or  (ii) one or more individual message/call application services; and  (b) is directed to a prescribed communications provider. Issue of international production order  (2) If the eligible Judge or nominated AAT member is satisfied, on the basis of the information given to the eligible Judge or nominated AAT member under this Division in connection with the application, that:  (a) in the case of an application for an international production order that is in respect of one or more individual transmission services—there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that:  (i) the prescribed communications provider owns or operates a telecommunications network that is, or is  Schedule 1  Amendments" ;
    skos:definition "criminal law Scope  (1) This clause applies if an interception agency applies, under clause 22, to an eligible Judge or nominated AAT member for an international production order that:  (a) is in respect of:  (i) one or more individual transmission services; or  (ii) one or more individual message/call application services; and  (b) is directed to a prescribed communications provider. Issue of international production order  (2) If the eligible Judge or nominated AAT member is satisfied, on the basis of the information given to the eligible Judge or nominated AAT member under this Division in connection with the application, that:  (a) in the case of an application for an international production order that is in respect of one or more individual transmission services—there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that:  (i) the prescribed communications provider owns or operates a telecommunications network that is, or is  Schedule 1  Amendments"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "24462eab4a6e9a50c00b5b11a4d7d1fc190bf8f2a1533f7b2c35e9cdc4775557" ;
    cof:pageNumber "55"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-30-2-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-30-2-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
