doc:sch-1-sec-82 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "82 Simplified outline of this Part" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "• International production orders may be issued for purposes in connection with the carrying out by the Organisation of its functions.  Amendments  Schedule 1 General amendments  Part 1  No. 78, 2021 Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production Orders) Act 2021  • There are 3 types of international production orders:  (a) international production orders relating to interception; and  (b) international production orders relating to stored communications; and  (c) international production orders relating to telecommunications data. • An international production order is directed to a prescribed communications provider. • An international production order may be issued in response to an application made by the Organisation. • An application for an international production order must nominate a designated international agreement. Note: An international production order comes into force when it is given to a prescribed communications provider under clause 112." ;
    cof:pageNumber "116"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-83 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "83 Application for international production order—national"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-83 ;
    values:originalText "security  (1) The Organisation may apply to a nominated AAT Security Division member for an international production order under clause 89 that:  (a) is in respect of:  (i) one or more individual transmission services; or  (ii) one or more individual message/call application services; and  (b) is directed to a prescribed communications provider.  (2) The application must nominate a designated international agreement.  Schedule 1  Amendments" ;
    skos:definition "security  (1) The Organisation may apply to a nominated AAT Security Division member for an international production order under clause 89 that:  (a) is in respect of:  (i) one or more individual transmission services; or  (ii) one or more individual message/call application services; and  (b) is directed to a prescribed communications provider.  (2) The application must nominate a designated international agreement.  Schedule 1  Amendments"@en ;
