concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-89 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "89 Issue of international production order—national security"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-89 ;
    values:originalText "Scope  (1) This clause applies if the Organisation applies, under clause 83, to a nominated AAT Security Division member for an international production order that:  (a) is in respect of:  (i) one or more individual transmission services; or  (ii) one or more individual message/call application services; and  (b) is directed to a prescribed communications provider. Issue of international production order  (2) If the nominated AAT Security Division member is satisfied, on the basis of the information given to the nominated AAT Security Division member under this Division in connection with the application, that:  (a) in the case of an application for an international production order that is in respect of one or more individual transmission services—there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that:  (i) the prescribed communications provider owns or operates a telecommunications network that is, or is likely to be, used to supply those individual transmission services; or  (ii) the prescribed communications provider supplies those individual transmission services; and  (b) in the case of an application for an international production order that is in respect of one or more individual message/call application services—there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that the prescribed communications provider provides those individual message/call application services; and  (ba) the person who made the application on behalf of the Organisation reasonably suspects that the prescribed  Schedule 1  Amendments" ;
    skos:definition "Scope  (1) This clause applies if the Organisation applies, under clause 83, to a nominated AAT Security Division member for an international production order that:  (a) is in respect of:  (i) one or more individual transmission services; or  (ii) one or more individual message/call application services; and  (b) is directed to a prescribed communications provider. Issue of international production order  (2) If the nominated AAT Security Division member is satisfied, on the basis of the information given to the nominated AAT Security Division member under this Division in connection with the application, that:  (a) in the case of an application for an international production order that is in respect of one or more individual transmission services—there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that:  (i) the prescribed communications provider owns or operates a telecommunications network that is, or is likely to be, used to supply those individual transmission services; or  (ii) the prescribed communications provider supplies those individual transmission services; and  (b) in the case of an application for an international production order that is in respect of one or more individual message/call application services—there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that the prescribed communications provider provides those individual message/call application services; and  (ba) the person who made the application on behalf of the Organisation reasonably suspects that the prescribed  Schedule 1  Amendments"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b073f6c68ef8721107fd9815b19b2c35ec111d526b75c2123d1111ba64424000" ;
    cof:pageNumber "123"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-89-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-89-ss-2 ;
