    cof:pageNumber "143"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-108 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "108 Content of international production order"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-108 ;
    values:originalText "Scope  (1) This clause applies to an international production order issued under clause 107. Content  (2) The order must be signed by the nominated AAT Security Division member who issued it.  (3) The order must set out the following:  (a) the date on which the order was issued;  (b) the name of the prescribed communications provider to whom the order is directed;  (c) the name of the designated international agreement nominated in the application for the order.  Amendments  Schedule 1 General amendments  Part 1  No. 78, 2021 Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production Orders) Act 2021  (4) If the order directs a prescribed communications provider to disclose telecommunications data to the Organisation, the order may require the provider to disclose that data to the Organisation in a specified way.  (5) A requirement under subclause (4) may:  (a) require that the telecommunications data be disclosed to the Organisation directly; or  (b) require that the telecommunications data be disclosed to the Organisation indirectly via the Australian Designated Authority.  (6) For the purposes of this clause, a specified way may deal with matters of timing. Example: If a requirement under subclause (4) relates to telecommunications data that commences to be held by a prescribed communications provider during a specified period, the requirement may require that the telecommunications data be disclosed to the Organisation within 30 minutes after the telecommunications data commences to be held." ;
    skos:definition "Scope  (1) This clause applies to an international production order issued under clause 107. Content  (2) The order must be signed by the nominated AAT Security Division member who issued it.  (3) The order must set out the following:  (a) the date on which the order was issued;  (b) the name of the prescribed communications provider to whom the order is directed;  (c) the name of the designated international agreement nominated in the application for the order.  Amendments  Schedule 1 General amendments  Part 1  No. 78, 2021 Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production Orders) Act 2021  (4) If the order directs a prescribed communications provider to disclose telecommunications data to the Organisation, the order may require the provider to disclose that data to the Organisation in a specified way.  (5) A requirement under subclause (4) may:  (a) require that the telecommunications data be disclosed to the Organisation directly; or  (b) require that the telecommunications data be disclosed to the Organisation indirectly via the Australian Designated Authority.  (6) For the purposes of this clause, a specified way may deal with matters of timing. Example: If a requirement under subclause (4) relates to telecommunications data that commences to be held by a prescribed communications provider during a specified period, the requirement may require that the telecommunications data be disclosed to the Organisation within 30 minutes after the telecommunications data commences to be held."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b073f6c68ef8721107fd9815b19b2c35ec111d526b75c2123d1111ba64424000" ;
    cof:pageNumber "146"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-108-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-108-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-108-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-108-ss-4 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-108-ss-5 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-108-ss-6 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf> ;
    dc:source "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf, p.146" .
doc:sch-1-sec-108 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "108 Content of international production order" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Scope  (1) This clause applies to an international production order issued under clause 107. Content  (2) The order must be signed by the nominated AAT Security Division member who issued it.  (3) The order must set out the following:  (a) the date on which the order was issued;  (b) the name of the prescribed communications provider to whom the order is directed;  (c) the name of the designated international agreement nominated in the application for the order.  Amendments  Schedule 1 General amendments  Part 1  No. 78, 2021 Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production Orders) Act 2021  (4) If the order directs a prescribed communications provider to disclose telecommunications data to the Organisation, the order may require the provider to disclose that data to the Organisation in a specified way.  (5) A requirement under subclause (4) may:  (a) require that the telecommunications data be disclosed to the Organisation directly; or  (b) require that the telecommunications data be disclosed to the Organisation indirectly via the Australian Designated Authority.  (6) For the purposes of this clause, a specified way may deal with matters of timing. Example: If a requirement under subclause (4) relates to telecommunications data that commences to be held by a prescribed communications provider during a specified period, the requirement may require that the telecommunications data be disclosed to the Organisation within 30 minutes after the telecommunications data commences to be held." ;
    cof:pageNumber "146"^^xsd:integer .

