doc:sch-1-sec-117-ss-4 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "117(4) Giving of instrument of revocation—the Organisation" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(4) If:  (a) an international production order is revoked under clause 116; and  (b) when the revocation takes effect, the Australian Designated Authority has not made a decision about the order under clause 112; clause 112 ceases to apply to the order when the revocation takes effect.  Amendments  Schedule 1 General amendments  Part 1  No. 78, 2021 Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production Orders) Act 2021" ;
    cof:pageNumber "154"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-118 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "118 Delegation by the chief officer of a relevant agency"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-118 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The chief officer of a relevant agency may, by writing, delegate any or all of the chief officer’s functions or powers under this Part to a certifying officer of the agency.  (2) In performing functions, or exercising powers, under a delegation under subclause (1), the delegate must comply with any directions of the chief officer." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The chief officer of a relevant agency may, by writing, delegate any or all of the chief officer’s functions or powers under this Part to a certifying officer of the agency.  (2) In performing functions, or exercising powers, under a delegation under subclause (1), the delegate must comply with any directions of the chief officer."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b4a19446558383c28b46db18e9d54815862f8ce643cfe55683a32c2352123b55" ;
    cof:pageNumber "155"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-118-ss-1 ;
