doc:sch-1-sec-126-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "126(3) Civil penalty provision—enforcement" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) For the purposes of Part 4 of the Regulatory Powers (Standard Provisions) Act 2014, the Federal Court of Australia and the Federal Circuit Court of Australia are relevant courts in relation to a civil penalty provision in this Part.  Schedule 1  Amendments" ;
    cof:pageNumber "159"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-127 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "127 Simplified outline of this Part"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-127 ;
    values:originalText "• The chief officer of a relevant agency and the Australian Designated Authority must give the Minister annual reports about matters relating to international production orders. • The Director-General of Security must give the Attorney-General a report on the extent to which compliance by a prescribed communications provider with an international production order has assisted the Organisation in carrying out its functions. • The Minister must cause to be prepared annual reports about matters relating to international production orders that were issued in response to applications made by relevant agencies. • The chief officer of a relevant agency, the Director-General of Security and the Australian Designated Authority must ensure that records are kept of matters relating to international production orders.  Amendments  Schedule 1 General amendments  Part 1  No. 78, 2021 Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production Orders) Act 2021" ;
    skos:definition "• The chief officer of a relevant agency and the Australian Designated Authority must give the Minister annual reports about matters relating to international production orders. • The Director-General of Security must give the Attorney-General a report on the extent to which compliance by a prescribed communications provider with an international production order has assisted the Organisation in carrying out its functions. • The Minister must cause to be prepared annual reports about matters relating to international production orders that were issued in response to applications made by relevant agencies. • The chief officer of a relevant agency, the Director-General of Security and the Australian Designated Authority must ensure that records are kept of matters relating to international production orders.  Amendments  Schedule 1 General amendments  Part 1  No. 78, 2021 Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production Orders) Act 2021"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "ee23996d817506c51e655c926752df416a74af1fa8826e674f6e338b484f9574" ;
    cof:pageNumber "160"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Annual reports must be given by certain agencies and authorities." ;
    dc:description "annual reports" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
