concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-140-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "140(3) Destruction of records"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-140-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) If:  (a) an international production order was issued in response to an application made by a relevant agency; and  (b) in compliance with the order, a prescribed communications provider makes a copy of stored communications available to the agency (whether directly or indirectly via the Australian Designated Authority); and  (c) the copy is in the agency’s possession; and  (d) the chief officer of the agency is satisfied that the copy is not likely to be required for a purpose referred to in clause 153 or 158; the chief officer must cause the copy to be destroyed immediately after becoming so satisfied." ;
    skos:definition "(3) If:  (a) an international production order was issued in response to an application made by a relevant agency; and  (b) in compliance with the order, a prescribed communications provider makes a copy of stored communications available to the agency (whether directly or indirectly via the Australian Designated Authority); and  (c) the copy is in the agency’s possession; and  (d) the chief officer of the agency is satisfied that the copy is not likely to be required for a purpose referred to in clause 153 or 158; the chief officer must cause the copy to be destroyed immediately after becoming so satisfied."@en ;
